- turbo_exempts_page_from_cache
/ A day grows with the timelines of its cars, and the live view with the
  lists and maps of its cars, so the window scrolls. A day that only the
  admin sees has a note in the middle instead (see Car::AdminOnlyDays).
  While the daily summaries build, a day has the progress bar in the middle
  as well, so the card does not wait for the frames of the progress bar.
- content_for :full_height, true if !timeframe&.now? && (!timeframe&.day? || admin_only_day? || @missing_or_stale_summary_days.present?)
/ The live view of a phone is a grouped list on gray (see Car::LiveCard)
- content_for :grouped, true if timeframe&.now?

- if @missing_or_stale_summary_days.present?
  = render 'shared/home_sub_nav', status: false
  = turbo_stream.update scoped_frame_id('timeframe') do
    = render Timeframe::Component.new(timeframe:)
  = render Summary::Builder::Component.new(timeframe:, missing_or_stale_days: @missing_or_stale_summary_days)

- elsif Sensor::HomePage.permitted?(page_key)
  - if stats?
    / With more than one car or with guest sessions, the select stays also
      for a timeframe with one car, so it does not come and go with the
      timeframe. The live view shows each car in use, with its name, so it
      needs no select. Below a wide screen, the choices are chips below the
      period.
    - if car_select? && !timeframe.now?
      - content_for :sub_nav_select do
        div id=frame_id('car-select')
          = render car_select_component
      - content_for :sub_nav_chips do
        div id=frame_id('car-select-chips')
          = render car_select_component(chips: true)
    = render 'shared/home_sub_nav', status: false

    / The sensors of a car report far less often than the sensors of the
      house, so the live view has no chart and refreshes less often
    - if timeframe.now?
      = render StatsWithChart::Component.new(sensor_name:, timeframe:, chart: false, min_interval: 30.seconds)

    / A recent day shows when the cars drove and charged, so a visitor gets a
      note in its place (see Car::AdminOnlyDays)
    - elsif admin_only_day?
      .flex-1.flex.items-center.justify-center.rounded-2xl.bg-surface.px-4
        = render Car::AdminOnlyDay::Component.new

    - elsif cars.empty? && !car_selection.guest?
      .flex-1.flex.items-center.justify-center.rounded-2xl.bg-surface.px-4
        = render Car::NoneInUse::Component.new(text: t('data.car_none_in_use'))

    / The figures of the charging and of the driving, and one chart. The
      desktop has the figures on the left and the chart on the right, a phone
      the chart below the figures. A day has its timeline in the place of the
      chart.
    - else
      / A period of a visitor ends with the latest public day, which a note
        above the figures says (see Car::AdminOnlyDays)
      - if admin_only_days_left_out?
        / On the desktop the banner undoes the padding of the card (see the
          layout)
        .mb-4.lg:-mx-6.lg:-mt-5.lg:mb-6
          = render Car::AdminOnlyNotice::Component.new(text: t('car_breakdown.admin_only_days_left_out'), banner: true)
      = render StatsWithChart::Component.new(sensor_name: chart_name, timeframe:, chart: chart_name.present?) do |pair|
        / A day grows with its timelines, so the window scrolls. On the
          desktop its cards have at least the height of a period.
        div class=['flex flex-1 flex-col gap-6 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2', (timeframe.day? ? 'lg:landscape:min-h-165' : 'min-h-0')] data=pair.refresh_options
          / Until the figures come, a placeholder in their layout keeps their
            place, so the chart does not move and draw itself again. The
            cards hold the figures of the charging and of the driving.
            Without an odometer, the card of the charging is the only one.
          = pair.stats_frame(['flex', driving? ? 'max-lg:h-80' : 'max-lg:h-52']) do
            = render Car::PeriodOverview::Component.new(driving: driving?)
          - if pair.chart?
            = pair.chart_frame('flex-1 min-h-48 flex relative')

          / The figures load the timeline with them (see the stats of the
            cars). Until it comes, a placeholder keeps its place. Like the
            figures, it is permanent: a refresh of the page keeps the figures
            and loads them not again, so it keeps the timeline too. On a
            phone, it takes the rest of the window, so a single timeline can
            fill it.
          - if timeframe.day?
            div id=scoped_frame_id('timeline') class='max-lg:flex-1 flex flex-col' data-turbo-permanent=true
              = render Car::DayTimeline::Component.placeholder
  - else
    = render Ui::Message::Component.new do |c|
      - c.with_watermark do
        = icon 'car'
      = c.with_title { t('layout.incomplete_car') }
      = c.with_body { raw t('layout.missing_car') }

- else
  = render DemoLink::Component.new feature: Sensor::HomePage.feature(page_key),
                                   url: { **permitted_params }
